{sec("white", f"""{split("", f"Client assets.<br>Accounted for{G}", "Safeguarding client assets is a continuing duty. In the UK, the FCA&rsquo;s Client Assets Sourcebook sets the rules for client money and safe custody assets.")}<div class="big3 mt"><div class="it rv"><b>CASS 7</b><h3>Client money</h3><p>Segregation, the statutory trust, acknowledgement letters from banks, records and reconciliations.</p></div><div class="it rv"><b>CASS 6</b><h3>Safe custody assets</h3><p>Safekeeping, ownership rights, records and reconciliations that separate client assets from the firm&rsquo;s own.</p></div><div class="it rv"><b>DFSA</b><h3>DIFC framework</h3><p>EMFI Capital (DIFC) Limited is endorsed to hold or control client assets under the DFSA&rsquo;s separate rules. These are not CASS.</p></div></div><p class="fine" style="margin-top:24px">These arrangements reduce specific custody risks. They do not protect investment performance or remove bank, custodian, depository or counterparty risk. {T("Compliance to map duties to entities and activities")}</p>""")}
{sec("navy", f"""{split("", f"Know what<br>you pay{G}", "A fee schedule should make the economics clear before you transact. The approved schedule, not this page, governs.")}<div class="ledger mt"><div class="lr rv"><strong>Custody</strong><span>Five tiers set by your Monthly Fee Balance (USD): under 5,000; 5,000 to 10,000; 10,000 to 15,000; 15,000 to 25,000; and 25,000 or more. The custody rate falls from 5 bps to 1 bp across the tiers.</span></div><div class="lr rv"><strong>Monthly minimum</strong><span>USD 2,500 per calendar month, a floor rather than an extra fee on top of DVP and custody. Minimum liquid assets USD 250,000.</span></div><div class="lr rv"><strong>DVP and tickets</strong><span>Ticket charges that fall with volume, set out in the schedule.</span></div><div class="lr rv"><strong>Third-party charges</strong><span>Depository, market and infrastructure charges, passed through where applicable.</span></div><div class="lr rv"><strong>Cash and other services</strong><span>Interest, account and service charges, and how they are calculated. EMFI does not pay interest on client cash.</span></div></div><p class="fine" style="margin-top:18px">All figures in USD unless stated. Not a quotation, and no comparison with any other provider is made. {T("Confirm every figure and the tier-by-tier rates against the approved current schedule before publishing")}</p>""")}
